\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Combined event-time path of road-quality and house-price RD coefficients. House-price coefficients (black, left axis, percent of mean) are flat in the pre-period and through $\tau = +3$, then open sharply between $\tau = +4$ and $\tau = +9$. Road-quality coefficients (blue bars, right axis on inverted scale, Road Quality Rating units) are reported for rolling 3-year post-election windows and become statistically detectable in the $\tau \in [2,4]$ window before peaking in the $\tau \in [3,5]$ window. The synchronization between the visibility of physical decay and the timing of the price response is the central piece of reduced-form evidence in this paper.}}{31}{figure.caption.22}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:combined_timeline}{{5}{31}{Combined event-time path of road-quality and house-price RD coefficients. House-price coefficients (black, left axis, percent of mean) are flat in the pre-period and through $\tau = +3$, then open sharply between $\tau = +4$ and $\tau = +9$. Road-quality coefficients (blue bars, right axis on inverted scale, Road Quality Rating units) are reported for rolling 3-year post-election windows and become statistically detectable in the $\tau \in [2,4]$ window before peaking in the $\tau \in [3,5]$ window. The synchronization between the visibility of physical decay and the timing of the price response is the central piece of reduced-form evidence in this paper}{figure.caption.22}{}}
